# Roof geometry contract

Before implementing or changing roof, rafter, purlin, elevation, datum, RoofPlane, seating, or schematic/section presentation code or tests, read the normative contract:

- [docs/geometry/roof-elevation-contract.md](../../docs/geometry/roof-elevation-contract.md)

That file (*Geometrický slovník KROVY v1.0*) is the single SSOT shared with Codex.

## Critical rules

- Accepted physical definitions, verified HOST elevation measurements, Core tests, Core implementation, and the contract must be mutually consistent. On contradiction: **stop and report**. Do not silently pick one source by list rank; an implementation bug does not override accepted HOST physical geometry.
- Core owns physical member positions, seating, Bottom/Center/Top, RoofPlane, datum resolution, and persisted geometry.
- WPF/SVG presentation renders and maps; it is not a geometry solver and is never technical-geometry authority.
- **Presentation-only changes must not modify physical technical elevations or persisted geometry.**
- Do not overwrite `ElevationProfile.BottomLocalZMm` / `CenterLocalZMm` / `TopLocalZMm` from SVG seating or visual contact coordinates.
- `*HostRegression*` test names are not themselves proof of a completed AutoCAD HOST retest.
- Do not reset, stash, commit, or push uncommitted WIP unless the user explicitly requests it.

Do not duplicate the full glossary here; link and follow the contract.
